Task: implement generic consumer stream supervision (Green phase), Phase
2 of purekafka (ADR 0010).

Added modules/purekafka/src/main/scala/purekafka/consumer/StreamSupervisor.scala:
- StreamSupervisorConfig(baseDelay, maxDelay) - explicit config, same
  style as Phase 1's RetryConfig/CircuitBreakerConfig, no hidden
  defaults.
- StreamSupervisor.nextDelay: pure delay-doubling-capped-at-maxDelay
  function, factored out so the cap/growth logic is testable without
  any real waiting.
- StreamSupervisor.supervise[F, O](config)(logger)(meter)(build: => F[Stream[F, O]]): Stream[F, O] -
  hand-rolled restart-with-backoff loop via Stream.eval/handleErrorWith/
  Stream.sleep, since no existing fs2/Typelevel combinator does this
  directly (Stream.retry retries a single effectful value, not a
  long-running stream). Takes the stream as a by-name F[Stream[F, O]]
  build action, not a plain Stream[F, O] value, since restarting means
  rebuilding from scratch (e.g. re-subscribing a Kafka consumer), not
  resuming a half-consumed stream. Deliberately unbounded attempts, no
  circuit breaker - matches spec.md's explicit decision (giving up
  recreates TD-2's exact symptom; there's no "downstream being hammered"
  concept on the consume side).
- Own purekafka.stream.restarts counter metric, same
  construct-once-reuse-many-times convention as Phase 1's
  purekafka.retry.attempts/purekafka.circuit_breaker.* metrics.

Required Async[F] rather than Temporal[F] as the type bound - Ref.unsafe
needs Sync[F], which Temporal alone doesn't provide (Temporal extends
Concurrent + Clock, not Sync); Async extends both Temporal and Sync, and
is what every other purekafka combinator already uses, so this keeps the
module's constraint consistent rather than introducing a second pattern.

